 <p class="note">Applicability: written for fixed-wing pilots of every service. The tactical procedures come from Navy and Marine Corps training (T-45 jets and tiltrotor students), the display limits from the UK military regulator, and the close configurations and signals from a civilian guide, all given in generic form with service rules labelled. Air Force (AFMAN 11-248) and Army fixed-wing four-ship guidance, and US military display-team procedures, could not be read for this revision. Your service’s rules, your unit’s standard procedures and the aircraft’s flight manual govern.</p>

